{
  "dom_id": "step-t6305",
  "name": "Equivalent Forms of the Central Limit Theorem",
  "problem": "Throughout this lesson, we've used the fact that if $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma,$ then for sufficiently large $n,$ \n\n$$\n\\overline{X}\\approx N\\!\\left(\\mu,\\frac{\\sigma^2}{n}\\right).\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the central limit in several different ways. Let's list some of the most common.\n\n- One way of restating the central limit theorem is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overline{X} - \\mu\\approx N\\!\\left(0,\\dfrac{\\sigma^2}{n}\\right).\n$$\n\nThis statement tells us that the deviation of $\\overline{X}$ from the mean $\\mu$ is (approximately) normally distributed with a mean of zero and a variance that's the same as $\\overline{X}.$\n\n- We can also write the central limit theorem as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\overline{X} - \\mu}{\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}}\\approx N\\!\\left(0,1\\right).\n$$\n\nThis statement tells us that $z$-scoring the sample mean gives a random variable that (approximately) follows a standard normal distribution.\n\n- Earlier, we saw that\n\n$$\nn\\overline{X} \\approx N\\!\\left(n\\mu,n\\sigma^2\\right).\n$$\n\nIf we $z$-score this result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{n\\overset{―}{X}-n\\mu }{\\sqrt{n{\\sigma }^{2}}} & =\\frac{n(\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu )}{\\sqrt{n}\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{n}(\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu )}{\\sigma }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that we can express the central limit theorem in the following form:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{n}(\\overline{X} - \\mu) }{\\sigma} \\approx N(0,1)\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t6305\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Equivalent Forms of the Central Limit Theorem</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t6305\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                           